# a SIN without its frequency into Xyce is an error (b6567bf5).
# What the fix was for, as the ledger has it: the source gives no frequency, which Xyce's sin( )
# needs: every value of the waveform is a loss and the source is written without it
from: ngspice
to: xyce
--- input
t
V1 a 0 SIN(0 1)
.tran 10n 1u
.end
--- output
t
V1 a 0
.tran 10n 1u
.end
--- report
error[loss]: line 2: vsource.wave = sine has no spelling in xyce
error[loss]: line 2: vsource.sinedc = 0 has no spelling in xyce
error[loss]: line 2: vsource.ampl = 1 has no spelling in xyce
warning[caveat]: line 3: tran.step: the first .TRAN number only sets the initial step in Xyce
